self|personal-identity|NOUN|person's own identity or character|A person's own identity, character, and inner experience.|bản thân; con người bên trong|The journal helped her understand her own self more clearly.|Cuốn nhật ký giúp cô ấy hiểu bản thân rõ hơn.|Countable in phrases such as one's true self; selves is the plural. This noun differs from reflexive pronouns such as herself.|0
wooden|made-of-wood|ADJECTIVE|made from wood|Made from wood.|bằng gỗ|A wooden bench stood under the old mango tree.|Một chiếc ghế dài bằng gỗ đặt dưới cây xoài già.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; this material sense differs from wooden meaning stiff or unexpressive.|0
councillor|council-member|NOUN|member of a local council|A member of a council that makes decisions for a local area.|thành viên hội đồng địa phương; nghị viên địa phương|The councillor listened to residents' concerns about the crossing.|Thành viên hội đồng địa phương lắng nghe lo ngại của cư dân về chỗ qua đường.|Countable; British spelling councillor, American councilor. Counsellor refers to a different role.|0
evaluate|assess|VERB|judge quality or value carefully|To consider evidence in order to judge the quality, value, or effectiveness of something.|đánh giá|The teachers evaluated the new timetable after a month.|Các giáo viên đánh giá thời khóa biểu mới sau một tháng.|Transitive evaluate something; evaluation may examine strengths and weaknesses, not only assign a score.|0
leading|prominent|ADJECTIVE|among the most important or successful|Among the most important, successful, or influential in a particular area.|hàng đầu; nổi bật|A leading researcher spoke at the public lecture.|Một nhà nghiên cứu hàng đầu phát biểu tại buổi diễn thuyết công cộng.|Usually before a noun; a leading person need not be the only leader or the person physically in front.|0
